title: "EchoROI: Scan-sector Segmentation and De-identification for Echocardiography"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23423164
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-02-21
url: "https://github.com/Kamlin-MD/UNET-Echocardiography-ROI-segmentation"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kamlin-MD/UNET-Echocardiography-ROI-segmentation"
abstract: >-
  EchoROI is a research Python package for U-Net-based scan-sector segmentation
  and masking in echocardiography images. It provides a command-line interface,
  a Python API, training and evaluation workflows, and Keras and ONNX model
  support. Masking pixels outside the predicted scan sector aids preprocessing
  and de-identification, but identifiers and overlays inside the sector may
  remain, and sector masking does not itself de-identify DICOM metadata.
  The accompanying technical manuscript is unrefereed; a software archive
  does not imply peer review.
  Pretrained weights are not distributed with this release because the
  contributing datasets have differing access and reuse conditions.
  Researchers must obtain source datasets independently from their providers.
  Requests for scan-sector annotations should be directed to the EchoROI
  authors; availability is assessed for each dataset under the applicable
  agreements and institutional permissions.
  Pretrained weights and source datasets are excluded from this release.
  The MIT licence applies to the released software, not source datasets or
  separately authorised annotation packages.
